{{Quote|The Empire's Inquisitors appear to have first dibs on these prototypes. Unusual for TIEs, the v1s have shields, hyperdrives, and folding wing panels... One of these fell into our hands after the action at Mustafar and Harinar's crew has had a merry time taking it apart.|[[Antoc Merrick]] in ''[[The Rebel Files]]''|<ref name="Rebel Files">''[[Star Wars: The Rebel Files]]''</ref>}}
The '''TIE/ad v1''', or '''TIE Advanced v1''', was an experimental [[TIE series|TIE fighter]] model of the [[Imperial Navy]].

==Description==
[[File:TIEAdvancedV1-USWNE.png|thumb|250px|left|A TIE/ad v1's s-foils folded when in landing configuration.]]
The TIE/ad v1 was heavily based off [[Sienar Fleet Systems|Republic Sienar Systems']] own ''[[Scimitar]]''. The [[starfighter]] was fitted with basic shields, and unlike the [[TIE Advanced x1]], the v1's [[S-foils]] could fold in around the cockpit when not in flight, conserving hangar space. Unusual for a [[TIE series|TIE model]], it had solar panels only on the inside surface of the wings with armor on the outside surfaces in order to make it more resistant to lateral enemy fire. This resulted in low power output from the panels, requiring the engines to run on fuel instead of the solar reactor, which only powered weapons, sensors, and auxiliary systems.<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> These engines were an upgrade on the standard ones used for the standard [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[TIE/ln space superiority starfighter|TIE/ln]].<ref name="Baron of the Empire">{{FFGXW2|set=Galactic Empire Conversion Kit|cardname=Baron of the Empire}}</ref> The TIE/ad v1 was armed with dual chin mounted [[laser cannon]]s, stronger than those of the [[TIE/ln space superiority starfighter]], and a [[projectile launcher]], used to fire [[Homing beacon|tracking devices]] like the [[XX-23 S-thread tracker]]. The TIE/ad v1 was also able to launch [[missile]]s.<ref name="One Year Later" /> Unlike most other TIE models, the v1 was outfitted with a [[hyperdrive]] and basic shields.<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> Overall, the TIE/ad v1 was an experimental and groundbreaking design<ref name="Baron of the Empire" /> that was held in high regard by the [[Imperial Navy]].<ref name="ED" />

==History==
{{Quote|And who better to take this beauty on her maiden voyage than one of the best imperial pilots on Lothal &mdash; Baron Valen Rudor.|[[Minister]] [[Maketh Tua]], revealing the TIE/ad v1 on Empire Day|<ref name="ED" />}}
[[File:The_Inquisitor_TIE_Adv_Prototype_XWM.png|thumb|left|250px|The Inquisitor's TIE/ad v1 pursuing rebels]]
The TIE/ad v1 was unveiled on [[Empire Day]], on the [[planet]] [[Lothal]], fifteen [[Standard year|years]] after the formation of the [[Galactic Empire]]. During the unveiling, it was announced that the TIE/ad v1 would be produced on Lothal by [[Sienar Fleet Systems]]. It was to be flown by [[Baron of the Empire|Baron]] [[Valen Rudor]]. Immediately after the unveiling, the TIE/ad v1 was destroyed by [[Kanan Jarrus]].<ref name="ED" />
During the same year, a pair of TIE/ad v1 starfighters were employed at [[Sienar Test Facility 73]], as part of [[Sienar Test Facility 73 defense battalion|the base’s defense]]. Both of these starfighters pursued and were destroyed by [[Cassian Jeron Andor]] as he made his [[Theft of the TIE Avenger prototype|escape]] in the stolen [[TIE Avenger prototype]]. Andor in the Avenger was able to dodge the TIE/ad v1 starfighters' missiles, and as he and his pursuers traversed through a canyon on [[73|Sienar 73]], he fired at an overhanging ledge with his own starship's missiles, resulting in the debris crushing the two Imperial TIEs.<ref name="One Year Later">{{Andor|One Year Later}}</ref>

[[The Grand Inquisitor]] was entrusted with a [[The Inquisitor's TIE Advanced|TIE Advanced v1]] of his own due to the sensitive nature of his top-secret missions in hunting down [[Jedi]]. This particular TIE was stolen by Kanan Jarrus and his [[Padawan]], [[Ezra Bridger]], when fleeing the [[Mustafar system]].<ref name="FATG" /> Afterward, it was given to the rebellion, where Major [[Capin Harinar]]'s unit analyzed it.<ref name="Rebel Files" />

Later on, both the [[Fifth Brother]] and the [[Seventh Sister]] also utilised TIE/ad v1s during a mission to the planet [[Takobo]] to recover a Force sensitive Ithorian baby. These particular fighters were destroyed by [[Garazeb Orrelios]] and [[C1-10P|Chopper]] when they found them in their hangar.<ref name="TFOTF">{{Rebels|The Future of the Force}}</ref> They received replacements soon after, and used them to pursue the [[Phoenix Cell]] Jedi to the [[Lothal Jedi Temple|temple]] on [[Lothal]].<ref name="SOD">{{Rebels|Shroud of Darkness}}</ref>

[[File:FifthBrother-SWZ.png|thumb|left|250px|The Fifth Brother arrives on Malachor.]]
The [[Eighth Brother]] also used a TIE/ad v1 to travel to [[Malachor]] and find [[Maul]]. It was later hijacked by Chopper, and then used by Maul to escape the planet.<ref name="TOTA">{{Rebels|Twilight of the Apprentice}}</ref>

After the [[Battle of Yavin]], [[Lindon Javes]] flew one as the flight lead of [[Helix Squadron]]. During the [[Battle at Fostar Haven]], he used ion torpedoes to disable his wingmates in order to save a [[Alderaanian refugee convoy|convoy of refugees]] from [[Alderaan]]. He then defected to the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|rebellion]] when [[Echo Squadron]] arrived.<ref name="Squadrons" />

==Behind the scenes==
''[[Star Wars Rebels: Head to Head]]'' gives the length of a TIE/ad v1 as 3.57 [[meter]]s, but ''[[Star Wars Rebels: Beware the Inquisitor!]]'' states that the Inquisitor's TIE measures 9.2 meters in length. This article assumes the former source is correct. The ''[[Star Wars: Imperial Handbook: A Commander's Guide]]'', which was developed prior to the reclassification of the Expanded Universe as [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] and is based almost entirely in that material, includes a mention of the v1 model.

